### 5.6 AI Parent Guide — `/parent/ai-guide`  ⭐ *Primary Meal Suggestion Hub*
**Purpose:** Interactive AI interface providing general everyday parenting guidance — **including personalized meal suggestions**.

| Component | Details |
|---|---|
| Child Context Selector | Optional: choose linked child to personalize guidance |
| Chat Interface | Message input, scrollable conversation history |
| AI Response Display | Visually distinct from official daycare records (different color, "AI Guide" label) |
| Disclaimer Banner | "This is general informational guidance. Not a medical or professional consultation." |
| Out-of-Scope Handling | AI responds within bounds; medical/psychological requests are gracefully redirected |
| Offline State | Clear message if AI service is unavailable; other app features still work |

> 🍽️ **Meal Suggestions — Full AI Meal Guide Feature**  
> The AI Parent Guide is the **primary home for personalized meal suggestions**. This section defines how meal suggestions work end-to-end within the AI Guide:
>
> #### Meal Suggestion Capabilities
>
> | Capability | Details |
> |---|---|
> | **Age-appropriate meal ideas** | "Suggest a healthy lunch for my 2-year-old" |
> | **Allergy-aware suggestions** | AI auto-reads child's allergy/dietary flags from profile (if child context is selected) and excludes forbidden ingredients |
> | **Complementary meals** | "Today [child] had porridge and boiled egg at daycare — suggest a complementary dinner" |
> | **Weekly home meal planning** | "Give me 5 dinner ideas for this week that balance what the daycare served" |
> | **Ethiopian/local food context** | AI can suggest culturally appropriate foods (injera-based meals, etc.) when child's regional context is provided |
> | **Snack ideas** | "What healthy snacks can I send with my child tomorrow?" — aligned with daycare's snack policy |
> | **Store-linked products** | When relevant, AI may mention "You can also find [product] in the Ankelba store" |
>
> #### Meal Suggestion UI Enhancements
>
> | Element | Details |
> |---|---|
> | **Quick Prompt Chips** | Pre-built prompt buttons below the chat input: "🥗 Suggest a meal", "🍎 Healthy snack ideas", "🍽️ This week's dinner plan", "🌿 Allergy-safe options" |
> | **Child Context Badge** | When a child is selected, a visible badge shows "Suggestions personalized for [Child Name] · Allergies: [list]" so the parent knows their profile is active |
> | **Meal Card Responses** | AI meal suggestions are shown as structured **Meal Cards** (not plain text) when possible: Meal name, key ingredients, estimated prep time, age suitability |
> | **Safety Disclaimer on Meals** | Under meal suggestions: "These are general ideas. Always check ingredients against your child's specific allergies. Consult your pediatrician for dietary medical advice." |
> | **"Try This at Daycare" Button** | For snack ideas: a shortcut to message the daycare caregiver/admin about incorporating a suggested snack (sends as a message via FR-COM-01) |
>
> #### Allergy Guard Logic (Important)
> - When a child is selected, the system passes allergy and dietary restriction data to the AI prompt context
> - The AI prompt is engineered to explicitly avoid suggesting foods containing flagged allergens
> - If a parent asks about a food that conflicts with recorded allergies, the AI flags the conflict
> - This does NOT replace medical advice — disclaimer remains always visible
> - Allergy data is never sent to the AI without the parent actively selecting the child as context (privacy, FR-AI-07)
>
> #### Scope Guardrails (SRS FR-AI-05 Compliance)
> | Request Type | AI Behavior |
> |---|---|
> | "Suggest a healthy meal for my toddler" | ✅ Answered with meal suggestion |
> | "My child has food poisoning, what medicine?" | ❌ Redirected: "Please consult a doctor. I can suggest bland recovery foods if helpful." |
> | "Is my child lactose intolerant?" | ❌ Redirected: "I'm not able to diagnose. A pediatrician can confirm. I can suggest dairy-free meal alternatives." |
> | "What's a good snack to send tomorrow?" | ✅ Answered with snack suggestions |

> **SRS Ref:** FR-AI-01 to FR-AI-10, FR-CH-03 (allergy data), UC-10, BR-07, NFR-PRV-05  
> ⚠️ **TBD:** AI provider, data minimization design (TBD-03)

